h no decisions to measure. They are also why review.risk reads medium. EmojiSearch.js itself is measured. Every one of the 21 changed files maps to a requirement (codeChanges: 0 unmapped). checks_skipped (13 checks skipped by configuration) is the baseline's configuration: every gate's delta against the baseline run is unchanged.","refs":[{"id":"test/bdiff/corpus/lifecycle/seq-emoji-ok.events","kind":"test"},{"id":"shell/plugins/emojis/EmojiSearch.js","kind":"file","line":49},{"id":"tests_pass","kind":"check"}],"severity":"info","title":"Disclosure coverage_unmeasured: the 16 unmeasured files are behaviour-comparison inputs, not code (informational)","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"review.effects is absent (disclosure effects_unavailable), so call-path statements come from reading the code, and no uncodified connection could be detected (the scope approximations say so); the absence of spec-gap candidates proves nothing here. filterEmojis has one caller, rebuildDisplay in Emojis.qml, which passes the limit 1000 (Emojis.qml:75); the harness runs that caller as written. No new state: groups is local to each call.","refs":[{"id":"review.effects.approximations","kind":"check"},{"id":"shell/plugins/emojis/Emojis.qml","kind":"file","line":75},{"id":"shell/plugins/emojis/EmojiSearch.js","kind":"file","line":60}],"severity":"info","title":"Analysis bounds: no change-effects analysis for JS/QML here","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"Evaluated 14319598 (this branch; no upstream pull request yet) = baseline quattro-proof 1e433732 (upstream quattro 035ce29f product code plus the proof layer) + 00bae6f1, the upstream-style commit (EmojiSearch.js and test/shell.d/emojis-test.sh only) + proof work: H41S and two menu variables, hazard and spec-conformance reviews (REVIEW-261004-WW11 records the code MC/DC and the hand probe), trace re-reviews of JATY, the harness emoji mode with 16 inputs, a witness test, the adapter's Verifies line for H41S, the fixed known issue and its evidence (the reproducer is test/shell.d/emojis-test.sh), and H41S's derived verification state. This round only the baseline moved (0c01de03 to 1e433732, upstream quattro 393a43d4 to 035ce29f): upstream did not touch the emoji files, Emojis.qml or the insert helper, and the baseline did not change JATY, the adapter or the EmojiSearch.js code_mcdc target, which already measured this change last round. The branch's changed product and test lines, H41S and the 16 inputs are byte-identical to the previous evaluation; only one baseline variable description (menu search ranking, not the emoji picker) differs underneath. The prepared description compares against quattro 8e02fc8, which has the same emoji files as 035ce29f.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/emojis/EmojiSearch.js","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"test/shell.d/emojis-test.sh","kind":"file","line":5},{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-EMOJI-SEARCH-INSIDE-WORD.yaml","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"test/node/emojisearch-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"SW-REQ-261004-H41S","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"Mirror composition: upstream-style change vs proof work, and what moved this round","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}}],"packageDigest":"sha256:86f481bfbf2faa4d68e273d10ee21f401ed3a782a8ba35139dd7705ce8871c44","packageIdentity":"epkg-8b651f5c6be34e42ff24db0dad9a9c53192355ac715ca8b14f09e86814290346","riskAssessment":{"level":"low","rationale":"One function reorders its matches; the match test is unchanged and every changed decision is MC/DC-covered. Pinned by the change's test and a behaviour comparison whose 12 differences are all classified intended with identical controls. The package's own risk reads medium only for the unmeasured .events data files. Not merge approval: 12 prevents_ready compat findings wait for a reviewer, and the live Qt picker is not driven in this package."},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-annotation.v1","suggestedTests":[{"forClaim":18,"rationale":"Pins which 1000 emojis a one-letter search shows, the only case where the shown set changes.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/emojis/EmojiSearch.js","kind":"file","line":71},{"id":"test/bdiff/corpus/lifecycle/seq-emoji-letter.events","kind":"test"}],"title":"Grid contents for a one-letter search"},{"forClaim":19,"rationale":"Drives Qt and the real key handler, which the node harness models.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/emojis/EmojiSearch.js","kind":"file","line":71},{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-emoji-insert","kind":"file"}],"title":"Live picker: type ok, Enter, read the clipboard the insert helper serves"}],"summary":"**What the change does.** Commit 00bae6f1 (our upstream-style change; no pull request opened yet) ranks emoji search matches: the search text as a whole keyword first, then as the start of a keyword, then inside a word, each group in file order; a keyword ends at any character that is not a letter (a character with a case), a digit or an apostrophe. Before, the picker listed matches in file order, so Enter picked an emoji whose keyword merely contained the text (ok gave the broken heart, key the pile of poo, tea the face with tears of joy). The rest of this branch at 14319598 is proof work (SW-REQ-261004-H41S, reviews, the fixed known issue, harness inputs, a witness test). This round only the baseline moved, to quattro-proof 1e433732 (upstream quattro 035ce29f); the emoji code did not.\n\n**Is the fix verified?** The audit verdict at head is pass; test results are current: 69/69 passed. The change's test fails on the 1e433732 product file and passes here (re-run). Code-level MC/DC measures EmojiSearch.js: all 7 changed decisions covered, no uncovered outcome (the package says 14/14 because it counts each decision twice, once per artifact). Three boolean assignments the engine does not count have masking MC/DC by a reviewed hand probe only.\n\n**Compatibility.** All four compat sources ran. 12 differential findings, not yet approved (prevents_ready; compatibility changes_found), each classified intended against H41S: the first emoji changes for ok, tea, fr, key, car, pen, red, man and mail; for e and o the shown 1000 change. Controls (no search text, a phrase, no match, cat) are identical. test_diff, mcdc_diff and removed_behavior report none.\n\n**Questions for a human.** Approve or reject each compat finding. Is a different 1000 for one-letter searches acceptable? The live Qt picker is not driven in this package.\n\n**Traceability.** All 21 changed files map to a requirement. No spec-gap candidates, but without change-effects analysis for JS/QML none could be detected.\n\n**Not caused by this change.** coverage_unmeasured (the .events inputs are data), checks_skipped and effects_unavailable inform only.\n\n**Readiness** is not_assessed; next decision human_judgement (compat_changes_unapproved), reviewer authority. Nothing here is an approval."}
